{"shortDescription":"Spot basis bids for soybeans firmed at processing sites in the western US Midwest on Monday, reflecting brisk demand for prompt deliveries of the oilseed as rainy weather slowed the harvest of new-crop supplies, merchandisers said.Basis values are quoted against CBOT futures in cents/bu:NOTE: 0 = O…","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Spot basis bids for soybeans firmed at processing sites in the western US Midwest on Monday, reflecting brisk demand for prompt deliveries of the oilseed as rainy weather slowed the harvest of new-crop supplies, merchandisers said."]},{"type":"list","children":[{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Soy basis bids were steady to weaker elsewhere, and the corn basis was mixed at Midwest elevators and processors, spot checks showed."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["A crushing facility in Sioux City, Iowa, was bidding $1 a bushel over the price of Chicago Board of Trade November soybean futures (SX26) for soybeans delivered through Friday, while the posted bid for soybeans delivered the following week was 15 cents below futures."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Similarly, a Des Moines, Iowa, soy processor was bidding 70 cents over futures for soybeans delivered this week, and 30 cents under futures for deliveries next week."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Nationally, the US soybean harvest was 12% complete by Sunday, ahead of the five-year average of 8%, the US Department of Agriculture said in a weekly progress report. However, in Iowa, the No. 2 soybean state, harvesting was 2% complete, lagging the five-year average of 5%."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["\"An extremely soggy week across much of Iowa made it difficult for farmers to get much fieldwork done, with heavy rainfall leading to flooding in some areas,” Iowa state agriculture secretary Mike Naig said in a statement."]}]},{"type":